DESCRIPTION:Basement VHS presents:\n\nIT (1990) ON VHS\n\nThe Master of Ho
 rror unleashes everything you were ever afraid of.\n\nIn 1960\, seven outc
 ast kids known as “The Losers’ Club” fight against an ancient shape-
 shifting alien who poses as a child-killing clown\, while also dealing wit
 h bullies and abusive parents. Thirty years later\, they reunite to stop t
 he creature once and for all when it returns to their hometown. The two-pa
 rt TV miniseries comes to the big screen courtesy of Basement VHS.\n\nIn-p
 erson Q&A with Director Tommy Lee Wallace to follow the screening.\n\nThis
  event has been postponed from its previously scheduled date on October 30
 th. All tickets for the original date are still valid and ticket-holders h
 ave been sent communications regarding refunds if necessary. If you did no
 t receive communication and cannot attend the new date\, please contact us
  before November 14th to receive a refund.\n\nBasement is an art collectiv
 e and VHS archive in the Mission District of San Francisco\, CA. They host
  a weekly film screening and radio show on Radio Valencia.\n\nTickets: htt
 ps://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20263?siteToken=d2atbcege5knqsavn
 tt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/it-on-vhs-ticke
 ts\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35142050/a5018a18-5534-4401-8b19-908cb577f674.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T195100Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/it-on-vhs-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comedy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
DTSTAMP:20261029T100747Z
UID:dothebay-18006637@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Stand-Up Comedy at the Balboa Theatre\n\nA Packed Lineup of sh
 orter sets for up and coming Bay Area comedians during the first half of t
 he show\, with an intermission to grab another beer or popcorn from the lo
 bby or that right on time bathroom break. The second half of the show feat
 ures national touring and veteran comediansWith surprise pop-in guest sets
 .\n\nA night of laughs in the Richmond District you will not want to miss!
 \n\nHeadliner Johana Coca\n\nJohana Coca is a Los Angeles–based stand-up
  comedian with Honduran roots\, raised in Portland\, Oregon. She is a regu
 lar at the Laugh Factory Hollywood\, has opened for Iliza Shlesinger and G
 ary Owen\, and was featured on Season 2 of Iliza’s Locals\, now streamin
 g on Amazon Prime Video. She also won the Bend Comedy Festival joke compet
 ition. She is one of 14 children\, so she is desperate for your love and a
 ttention. Rooted in family\, culture\, and lived experience\, Johana turns
  personal stories into instantly relatable comedy. Her warmth and timing m
 ake every set feel like a conversation you don’t want to end with the co
 olest cousin you wish you had.\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.
 com/purchase/20219?siteToken=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://
 dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/comedy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35182689/e66cfb79-f62b-4cec-8ace-a7eae140b3f0.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T100747Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/comedy-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639487@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:“Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)\n
 Lindy in the Park\nGet ready to swing in Golden Gate Park every sunny Sund
 ay at “Lindy in the Park\,” a weekly free event near the de Young Muse
 um\, when the streets of Golden Gate Park are closed to traffic and the da
 ncers take over.\nThis in person event resumed June 20\, 2021\nLindy in th
 e Park | Free Outdoor Swing Dance & Lessons\nEvery Sunday | 11 am to 2 pm\
 nJFK Dr. btwn 8th and 10th\, behind the De Young Museum\, Golden Gate Park
 \, SF\nFREE\nRain and Bay to Breakers cancels\, but other than that\, Lind
 y in the Park takes place every Sunday – even on holidays – so even if
  New Year’s Day\, Christmas\, or Fourth of July falls on a Sunday\, they
 ’ll be out there dancing. On the very rare occasion when they cancel\, t
 hey’ll make a new posting on their website\, usually by 10am on Sunday. 
 Lindy in the Park’s Schedule FAQ\n\nFree Beginners Swing Lessons | Noon 
 to 12:30 pm\nLindy in the Park offers a free weekly beginning swing dance 
 lesson\, taught by Hep Jen. The lessons are short\, easy and fun and then 
 you can practice your new steps with the whole group until 2 pm.\nNo partn
 er is required\, as they rotate leaders and followers throughout the lesso
 n.\nUpdated 7/8/2021 – Event info last checked via website.\n\nUpcoming 
 “Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park) Events\nSun 1
 0/11 “Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)Sun 10/18
  “Lindy in the Park” Swing Dance Party (Golden Gate Park)Sun 10/25 “
 Lindy in the Park” Swing D...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: http://www.lindyinthep
 ark.com/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lindy-in-the-park-swing-dance-p
 arty-golden-gate-park-280/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/201608
 21-LITP20TH-321.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:JFK Drive Lindy Hop Spot\, JFK Dr. & Music Concourse Dr\, San Fra
 ncisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/lindy-in-the-park-swing-dance-party-golden-gat
 e-park-280/
END:VEVENT
