SUMMARY:Amy Oppenheimer’s Looking For Justice (In All The Wrong Places)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T181500
DTSTAMP:20261127T123954Z
UID:funcheap-1644115@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theater Performance
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerAmy Oppenheimer’s Looking Fo
 r Justice (In All The Wrong Places)\nWritten & Performed by: Amy Oppenheim
 er\nDirector: David Ford\nPerformance Coach: Julia McNeal\n5:00 pm Sundays
 \, November 29 – December 13\, 2026.\n\nThe Marsh Berkeley will present 
 an encore run of lawyer and retired judge Amy Oppenheimer’s seminal work
  Looking for Justice (In All the Wrong Places). Praised by Culture Vulture
  for its “acute honesty\, shrewd intelligence\, soft humor\, and more th
 an a bit of poignancy\,” and by 48Hills as “a refreshing type of epiph
 any\,” Looking for Justice (In All the Wrong Places) takes audiences ins
 ide Oppenheimer’s early career and trailblazing advocacy. Now safely bey
 ond the statute of limitations\, her stories unspool alongside a second jo
 urney: her own awakening as a lesbian feminist newly arrived in the Bay Ar
 ea. Built around a defining early case\, the show moves through a gripping
 \, looping narrative that shifts between quick-witted\, fast-talking pundi
 try and warm humor.\nContent Advisories: sexual violence/rape\, sexual har
 assment\, racism and familial violence.\n\n$25.00\n\nTickets: https://even
 tvesta.com/events/168649/t/tickets\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/amy-o
 ppenheimers-justice-wrong-places/\nSource: Funcheap SF
