 n\nTitles are listed alphabetically\, not in their screening order.\n\nArt
 ichoke (14 Minutes)\n\nHeld captive\, Cynara discovers a phoropter that op
 ens a portal to another world. In a terrifying cat-and-mouse chase between
  realities\, Cynara finally comes face to face with her oppressor and must
  decide what she’s willing to destroy in order to survive.\n\nThe Cabin 
 (28 Minutes)\n\nA car thief steals the wrong Limo\; and gets roped into br
 eaking into a paradoxical interstitial zone.\n\nClipping (6 Minutes)\n\nA 
 plant shop owner struggles to keep his business afloat while juggling hagg
 lers and thieves.\n\nEating in My Car Again (4 Minutes)\n\nA music video f
 or the song "Eating in My Car Again" by Greg Roensch.\n\nHalf & Half (7 Mi
 nutes)\n\nA man interviews for a job with all the right qualifications... 
 all except one...\n\nInto The Static (7 Minutes)\n\nHarry Loving is obsess
 ed with his life-simulation video game\, especially his digital companion\
 , Delilah. Isolated in his apartment\, the game becomes his reality\, and 
 begins consuming his every waking breath. Now\, Harry must choose between 
 the real world or disappearing forever into a pixelated fantasy with Delil
 ah.\n\nMINE (9 Minutes)\n\nSee You Next Tuesday (13 Minutes)\n\nA frustrat
 ed tech worker becomes obsessed with heckling a busking marionette artist.
