BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AHITH FEST 2026: The Haunting of Pennhurst
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T170000
DTSTAMP:20261127T014655Z
UID:dothebay-18082069@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:At a former institution for people with disabilities\, a haunt
 ed attraction employs disabled performers who confront the site’s abusiv
 e past while reclaiming its story on their own terms.\n\nOn the grounds of
  the former Pennhurst State School and Hospital\, where generations of peo
 ple with intellectual and developmental disabilities endured neglect and a
 buse\, a haunted attraction now draws thousands of visitors each year. But
  The Haunting of Pennhurst is less interested in cheap scares than in what
  it means to turn a site of real suffering into entertainment. Following t
 he disabled and neurodivergent performers who bring the attraction to life
 \, the documentary reveals a haunt shaped by unusually deliberate rules. A
 ctors are encouraged to build characters from their own experiences\, whil
 e slurs\, mockery\, and violence that recreates historical abuse are stric
 tly off-limits. For some performers\, stepping into the role of “monster
 ” becomes an act of reclamation in a place once designed to segregate pe
 ople like them. Yet the contradictions remain. Archival footage\, survivor
  testimony\, and the site’s museum continually return the film to Pennhu
 rst’s brutal history\, raising difficult questions about memory\, exploi
 tation\, education\, and who gets to tell the story of a place built on su
 ffering. Immersive and unsettling with an original score by Dan Deacon\, t
 he film leaves space for viewers to decide whether Pennhurst’s new life 
 is catharsis\, commerce\, or something more complicated.\n\nPlayi...\n\nTi
 ckets: https://www.balboamovies.com/calendar-of-events/ahith-2026-the-haun
 ting-of-pennhurst\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/13/ahith-f
 est-2026-the-haunting-of-pennhurst-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7760419;-122.498063
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35520868/260537df-861f-4966-8f35-769d565ed10b.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261127T014655Z
LOCATION:Balboa Theater\, 3630 Balboa St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/13/ahith-fest-2026-the-haunting-of
 -pennhurst-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mrs. Claus & The Naughty Ones
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261213T180000
DTSTAMP:20261127T014655Z
UID:dothebay-18069374@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Mrs. Claus & The Naughty Ones transforms a working San Francis
 co maker space into Mrs. Claus's North Pole workshop for an intimate\, imm
 ersive Christmas gathering on December 13.\n\nCreated by San Francisco art
 ist and immersive-event producer Indy\, the evening reimagines Mrs. Claus 
 not simply as Santa's wife\, but as the woman running a strange\, playful 
 Christmas world of her own.\n\nApproximately 100-125 guests will step insi
 de a functioning holiday workshop populated by Mrs. Claus and her cast of 
 Christmas characters and elves. Throughout the space\, guests can decorate
  cookies\, make ornaments\, take holiday portraits\, share a Christmas mea
 l\, and bring new toys for a Toys for Tots drive. Workshop elves will rece
 ive\, organize and wrap those donated toys throughout the evening\, making
  the charitable drive part of the immersive world itself.\n\nThe project b
 lends queer theatricality\, character performance\, community gathering an
 d immersive design while keeping the scale intentionally intimate. Rather 
 than presenting a traditional stage show\, Mrs. Claus & The Naughty Ones i
 nvites guests to enter the story and spend an evening inside it.\n\nAt the
  center is a simple reinterpretation of a familiar Christmas figure: Mrs. 
 Claus is no longer merely remembered in relation to Santa. In this worksho
 p\, she is the author of her own legend.\n\nEvent: Mrs. Claus & The Naught
 y Ones\nDate: December 13\, 2026\nLocation: San Francisco\nPresented by: I
 NDY EVENTS / Indy Gill\nFormat: Private immersive holiday gath...\n\nFree\
 nIndy\n\nTickets: https://partiful.com/e/qmf3hQtOZLdaDUIrleZV?\nDetails: h
 ttps://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/13/mrs-claus-the-naughty-ones-tickets\n
 Source: DoTheBay
