DESCRIPTION:When a family gathers at their condemned home for a reunion\, 
 they begin to unravel as toxic fumes from a nearby oil derrick affect them
  in ways they could never have fathomed. The oil causes them to become you
 nger\, but it also causes them to lose their memories.\n\nFor Matilda is t
 he feature film directorial debut of award winning auteur Brandon Doo.\n\n
 + 1 Short Film\n\nThe Wedding (14 Minutes)\n\nRay’s brother Tommy is liv
 ing with dementia and can no longer take care of himself. Hoping to keep h
 im at home and surrounded by people he knows\, Ray convinces their friend 
 Sarah to marry Tommy\, that way she can live with him and become his careg
 iver. But on the day of the wedding\, Ray’s son Eric arrives just in tim
 e to object to the union\, convinced that his Uncle Tommy no longer unders
 tands what he is agreeing to. Now Ray must convince Eric that the marriage
  isn’t an exploitation of Tommy’s condition but an act of love intende
 d to preserve what remains of his independence.\n\nPlaying as part of Anot
 her Hole in the Head 2026\n\nTickets: https://www.balboamovies.com/calenda
 r-of-events/ahith-2026-for-matilda\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2
 026/12/13/ahith-fest-2026-for-matilda-1-short-film-tickets\nSource: DoTheB
 ay
