CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Before the hockey mask\, there was the sack. Jason Voorhees re
 turns to the big screen on 16mm film!\n\nFive years after the massacre at 
 Camp Crystal Lake\, a new group of young counselors arrives at a nearby tr
 aining camp\, unaware that something sinister is lurking in the surroundin
 g woods. As the bodies begin to pile up\, a terrifying new killer emerges 
 from the shadows\, carrying on the bloody legacy of Crystal Lake.\n\nDirec
 ted by Steve Miner\, Friday the 13th Part 2 (1981) is one of the most belo
 ved entries in the legendary horror franchise. Featuring suspenseful kills
 \, an unforgettable final girl\, and Jason Voorhees in his original sack-m
 ask appearance\, this sequel helped establish the formula that would defin
 e slasher cinema throughout the 1980s.\n\nFor this special Another Hole in
  the Head Film Festival screening\, we're bringing Jason back to the big s
 creen projected from an authentic vintage 16mm film print. Experience the 
 gritty atmosphere\, old-school practical effects\, and unmistakable charm 
 of watching a horror classic on real celluloid.\n\nPlaying as part of Anot
 her Hole in the Head 2026\n\nTickets: https://www.balboamovies.com/calenda
 r-of-events/ahith-2026-friday-the-13th-part-2\nDetails: https://dothebay.c
 om/events/2026/12/16/ahith-fest-2026-friday-the-13th-part-tickets\nSource:
  DoTheBay
