BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LIVE MUSIC: Country Risquè\, Samantha Henson\, Sam Hirst
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T220000
DTSTAMP:20261127T014655Z
UID:dothebay-18070964@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Country Risquè\n\n(Special Dolly Parton Tribute feat. Sadie A
 lan)\n\nSince making their live debut in 2022\, Country Risqué has become
  something of a San Francisco queer country institution. Singer-songwriter
 s Miles Gordon and Daniel Bromfield first met in Eugene\, Oregon nearly a 
 decade before forming the band\, and after passing around songwriting idea
 s during the pandemic\, they reconvened in San Francisco and formed a honk
 y-tonk band centered around the coffee-and-chocolate contrast of Gordon’
 s rich\, formally trained vocals and Bromfield’s languid deadpan. As the
  band has developed\, its sound has progressed from a classic ‘50s-influ
 enced country style to a rougher and more electrified sound inspired by al
 t-country\, heartland rock and the rugged landscapes of the Pacific Northw
 est.\n\nCountry Risqué has had the privilege of sharing the stage with Li
 lly Hiatt\, Paisley Fields\, Ty Walker and the Humanoids\, Secret Emchy So
 ciety\, and countless other country and many other Americana luminaries. I
 t currently features Richard Moog on lead guitar\, Chris Kenyon on drums\,
  and Sarah Parker on bass.\n\nBandcamp | IG\n\nSamantha Henson\n\n(Full Ba
 nd)\n\nInspired by dive bars and romantic comedies\, Samantha Henson’s s
 ongs are rooted in folklore and storytelling with nostalgic warmth and bit
 tersweet humor\, and with an occasional tinge of psychedelia. This is all 
 because she draws inspiration from the greatest of the great folk legends:
  Blaze Foley\, Townes Van Zandt\, Nick Drake\, The Beatles\, and Jim Croce
 ....\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20410?siteTok
 en=d2atbcege5knqsavntt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/1
 2/18/live-music-country-risque-samantha-henson-sam-hirst-tickets\nSource: 
 DoTheBay
GEO:37.782364;-122.482951
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35452060/1089849a-93ed-4ce5-a56a-1c1a7429859a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261127T014655Z
LOCATION:4 Star Theater\, 2200 Clement St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94121
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/18/live-music-country-risque-saman
 tha-henson-sam-hirst-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Balboa Christmas Halloween Mystery Marathon ~ First Film
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T183000
DTSTAMP:20261103T193658Z
UID:dothebay-18017447@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Due to forces beyond our control\, we are no longer able to ru
 n the Balboa Halloween Mystery Marathon on Halloween night. In the circums
 tance\, we are hard pivoting to the Balboa Christmas Halloween Mystery Mar
 athon. Same exact run of show\, same exact films selected. Only with more 
 holiday vibes.\n\nThis year\, the Balboa invites you to the BALBOA CHRISTM
 AS HALLOWEEN MOVIE MARATHON.\n\nJoin us any time that evening for the low\
 , low price of $13 as four different programmer select one of their favori
 te horror gems and we run them back to back throughout the night. You won
 ’t know what we’re playing until it’s being announced in the theater
 \, but we can guarantee that all of the films are (a) pre-20th century\, (
 b) never screened in the Bay Area (at least in the past five years)\, and 
 (c) have one curator on our team who think it’s sick as hell. Along with
  that\, we’ll have hot chocolate\, candy canes and special prizes for a 
 mid-way point costume contest for anyone who wants to dress up! Whether yo
 u join for one or stay for all\, come with friends or alone\, we guarantee
  your Saturday at the Balboa will be a night of pure\, sugar high\, blood 
 soaked movie adrenaline.\n\n4:30 PM: Mystery Movie #1 (1979) (4:30 PM - 6 
 PM)\n\n6:10 PM: Mystery Movie #2 (1984) (6:05 PM - 7:30 PM)\n\nCostume Con
 test/Intermission (Fifteen Minutes)\n\n7:40 PM: Mystery Movie #3 (1988) (7
 :45 - 9:11 PM)\n\n9:15 PM: Mystery Movie #4 (1986) (9:15 PM - 10:38 PM)\n\
 n$13\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/20344?siteTok
 en=52wkfzmjpwjjfpz3ye7tz8wscg\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/1
 2/19/balboa-christmas-halloween-mystery-marathon-first-film-tickets\nSourc
 e: DoTheBay
